@copilot Update this PR directly with one remaining bridge-specific documentation correction; do not create a separate follow-up PR. The delivered bridge deprecations and caller replacements are present and should remain unchanged.

The unchanged Java8BytecodeBridge section in .github/agents/knowledge/javaagent-advice-patterns.md still instructs authors to use the bridge directly in annotated advice and says source-level inline = false does not create an exception because the transformer controls inlining. This contradicts this PR's updated .github/instructions/javaagent.instructions.md, the new deprecation Javadoc, and the migrated non-inlined callers. Update only that bridge-specific section to recommend direct OpenTelemetry APIs for non-inlined advice and ordinary helpers, state that Java8BytecodeBridge is deprecated, and retain the pre-Java-8 static-interface-call caveat: genuinely inlined advice needs a Java-8-compiled helper or conversion to non-inlined advice rather than blindly substituting static interface calls. Remove the stale transformer-overrides-inline claim there. Keep this concise and do not recommend new calls to either deprecated bridge.

Broader indy-first policy is being handled separately by existing PR #20827. Do not duplicate its broader article or contributor-guide rewrite, change runtime code, remove compatibility methods, or expand the cleanup. Acceptance: the bridge-specific knowledge section no longer contradicts this PR's deprecation and direct-call guidance. Use the existing repository Markdown validation for the changed file and report any concrete blocker. No runtime build is needed for this documentation-only correction.
